OL,3,GNEWSASecond arrest after fire destroys
OL,4,AGatwick passengers' cars
OL,5,
OL,6,FA second man has been arrested after a
OL,7,Ffire destroyed about 140 vehicles at a
OL,8,Fcar park used by passengers travelling
OL,9,Ffrom Gatwick Airport.
OL,11,FA 29-year-old man was arrested on
OL,12,FMonday, and has been released on bail
OL,13,Falongside a 67-year-old man who was
OL,14,Fheld on Saturday evening, when the fire
OL,15,Ftook place, Sussex Police said.
OL,17,FMeanwhile, Gatwick passengers who
OL,18,Fparked their car with a third party
OL,19,Fcompany that uses the site have
OL,20,Fcriticised a lack of communication,
OL,21,Fwith some yet to find out if their
OL,22,Fvehicle is safe, or has been destroyed.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
